PART 1 — HUMAN IDEA TO OMNI PROMPT PIPELINE
Converting an abstract human concept into a production-ready generative prompt for Google Omni 1.1 Flash (gemini-omni-1.1-flash) requires a deterministic prompt compilation pipeline1. Generative video models process natural language by mapping linguistic syntax directly to spatial-temporal representations1. Ambiguity, structural omissions, or syntax conflicts in the input prompt increase generation variance, leading to visual artifacts, temporal drift, or loss of creative intent1.
The prompt compilation pipeline systematically converts brief human inputs into detailed production descriptions. Each execution stage refines the narrative concept into explicit control instructions optimized for the multimodal architecture of Gemini Omni 1.1 Flash1.
Pipeline Stage Execution and Evidence Classification
    1. Human Idea Ingestion: The system ingests raw, unstructured text inputs provided by the user (for example, "A huge black cat walks through an abandoned hospital at night").
    2. Intent & Core Entity Understanding: The pipeline parses narrative goals, primary subjects, essential actions, and spatial settings.
        ◦ Evidence Level: A — OFFICIAL. Google explicitly directs prompt construction to begin with clear scene descriptions, core subject definition, and primary environmental setup1.
    3. Subject & Attribute Extraction: The system isolates the primary visual subject and defines its physical features, proportions, materials, scale, and surface textures relative to the scene.
        ◦ Evidence Level: A — OFFICIAL. Google documentation specifies including detailed subject attributes to anchor visual fidelity1.
    4. Action & Motion Vector Extraction: Verbs in natural language are expanded into physical motion vectors, directions, velocities, and mechanics.
        ◦ Evidence Level: A — OFFICIAL. Official documentation mandates granular motion descriptions rather than vague movement terms1.
    5. Environment & Spatial Framing: The engine defines spatial boundaries, architectural elements, background depth, atmospheric conditions, and floor planes.
        ◦ Evidence Level: A — OFFICIAL. Google documentation establishes environmental details as core components of effective video prompts1.
    6. Camera Dynamics & Composition Architecture: The pipeline sets framing, camera placement, tracking paths, focal parameters, and spatial composition.
        ◦ Evidence Level: A — OFFICIAL. Google explicitly instructs users to specify camera movements, angles, and framing techniques for optimal visual control1.
    7. Lighting & Visual Style Specification: Illumination sources, directionality, shadows, color palettes, and rendering medium parameters are established.
        ◦ Evidence Level: A — OFFICIAL. Documented by Google as critical criteria for driving model photorealism and stylistic coherence1.
    8. Native Audio Architecture: Acoustic soundscapes, physical sound effects (SFX), spoken dialogue, or musical score instructions are structured into the prompt payload.
        ◦ Evidence Level: A — OFFICIAL. Omni 1.1 Flash natively processes and generates synchronized audio alongside video based on text descriptions1.
    9. Temporal & Sequential Logic Check: Multi-action sequences are mapped to temporal markers across the shot duration to prevent visual overlapping.
        ◦ Evidence Level: B — INFERRED. Derived from keyframe interpolation and scene extension documentation requiring logical temporal continuity1.
    10. Model Capability & Parameter Validation: The prompt payload is validated against Omni 1.1 Flash limits, such as the maximum 10-second single-shot duration, supported aspect ratios of 16:9 and 9:16, and resolution settings (360p, 720p, 1080p, 4k)1.
        ◦ Evidence Level: A — OFFICIAL. Parameters are defined in the official Google API schemas1.
    11. Contradiction Detection & Complexity Pruning: The prompt is scanned for conflicting instructions (such as macro focus paired with wide landscape vistas) and non-descriptive buzzwords.
        ◦ Evidence Level: B — INFERRED. Inferred from official prompting guides advising against vague, overlapping, or conflicting descriptors1.
    12. Final Prompt Assembly & Production Output: Structural components are concatenated into a unified string formatted for ingestion by gemini-omni-1.1-flash1.
