PART 17 — CREDIT-SAVING ITERATION AND GENERATION STRATEGY
Generating high-resolution AI video requires managing computational resources efficiently. Randomly editing entire prompts upon experiencing an imperfect generation wastes credits and makes it difficult to identify what fixed the issue2.
A credit-efficient workflow follows five sequential operational phases:
    1. Phase 1 (Draft Generation): Dispatch initial compiled prompt at 360p draft resolution, capturing speed up to 60% faster at one-third API credit cost2.
    2. Phase 2 (Failure Analysis): Inspect low-resolution draft render to isolate single primary visual defect.
    3. Phase 3 (Variable Isolation): Modify only the specific prompt parameter responsible for observed failure.
    4. Phase 4 (Draft Re-verification): Re-render modified prompt at 360p to verify parameter fix.
    5. Phase 5 (Production Render): Upscale verified prompt output directly to 1080p or 4K resolution2.
Official Evidence vs. Engineering Strategy
    • Official Google Control (Level A): Google officially documents 360p resolution draft mode, demonstrating that it renders up to 60% faster at one-third the cost of standard 720p generation2. Google also supports upscaling finalized drafts directly to 1080p or 4K2.
    • Engineering Refinement Strategy (Level B): The single-variable iteration protocol (Draft 360p -> Isolate -> Fix Variable -> Verify 360p -> Final 4K Upscale) is a resource-management system designed to maximize daily credit yield2.
